Norm((768,), eps=1e-05, elementwise_affine=True)\n","      (mlp): GPT2MLP(\n","        (c_fc): Conv1D(nf=3072, nx=768)\n","        (c_proj): Conv1D(nf=768, nx=3072)\n","        (act): NewGELUActivation()\n","        (dropout): Dropout(p=0.1, inplace=False)\n","      )\n","    )\n","  )\n","  (ln_f): LayerNorm((768,), eps=1e-05, elementwise_affine=True)\n",")"]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":3}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["This step prepares a simple input sentence that will be fed into the model. The string “Paris is the capital of France” is tokenized using the GPT-2 tokenizer, which converts the text into numerical tokens the model can understand. The return_tensors='pt' argument ensures that the output is returned as PyTorch tensors, the format required by the model. From this, the input_ids are extracted, which represent the encoded token IDs of the sentence and will be used as the model’s direct input during the interpretability analysis."],"metadata":{"id":"FZPaBdiMuQeM"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Prepare example sentence\n","sentence = \"Paris is the capital of France\"\n","inputs = tokenizer(sentence, return_tensors='pt')\n","input_ids = inputs['input_ids']"],"metadata":{"id":"J574XQlel4_o","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1757427875362,"user_tz":-420,"elapsed":28,"user":{"displayName":"Harriet","userId":"08169952984174915407"}}},"execution_count":4,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["This part of the code runs the sentence through GPT-2 and then visualises the internal activations of the model. When the inputs are passed into the model, the outputs.last_hidden_state contains the hidden representations for each token at the final layer. These are detached from the computation graph and converted into a NumPy array for easier manipulation. The heatmap created with Seaborn shows how each token in the sentence is represented across the model’s embedding dimensions, with tokens along the x-axis and embedding dimensions along the y-axis. This kind of visualisation is a core mechanistic interpretability technique, allowing us to see how the model encodes and distributes information internally for a given input."],"metadata":{"id":"ECtIk3xmuW9m"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Mechanistic Interpretability: Visualise model activations\n","outputs = model(**inputs)\n","activations = outputs.last_hidden_state.detach().squeeze().numpy()\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n","sns.heatmap(activations.T, cmap=\"viridis\", xticklabels=sentence.split())\n","plt.xlabel('Token')\n","plt.ylabel('Embedding Dimension')\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":548},"id":"NQExumsDl6t0","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1757427876778,"user_tz":-420,"elapsed":1415,"user":{"displayName":"Harriet","userId":"08169952984174915407"}},"outputId":"96d33edf-02e9-42cc-f886-65287c9b3650"},"execution_count":5,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["This section extends the interpretability exercise by applying Integrated Gradients to highlight which input tokens contribute most strongly to the model’s predictions. Unlike the earlier step that only visualised activations, here we load GPT-2 with its language modelling head (GPT2LMHeadModel) so it can produce prediction scores over the vocabulary. A wrapper function called predict is defined to compute a scalar output based on the summed logits of the final token, which provides a target for attribution.\n","\n","The embeddings for the input sentence are then extracted directly from the model’s embedding layer, and Integrated Gradients is applied to calculate attribution scores for each token. These scores quantify how much each token’s embedding influences the model’s final prediction. To make the results interpretable, the attributions are summed across embedding dimensions, leaving one attribution score per token. Finally, the Captum visualization module generates a saliency map that overlays attribution values on the original words, producing an intuitive view of which parts of the input text the model relied on most heavily in forming its output."],"metadata":{"id":"vLGT11Whud3x"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Saliency Map with Integrated Gradients\n","from transformers import GPT2LMHeadModel\n","from captum.attr import IntegratedGradients, visualization\n","\n","# Reload GPT-2 with a language modeling head for prediction scores\n","lm_model = GPT2LMHeadModel.from_pretrained(model_name)\n","lm_model.eval()\n","\n","# Define prediction wrapper for Integrated Gradients\n","def predict(input_embeds):\n","    outputs = lm_model(inputs_embeds=input_embeds)\n","    logits = outputs.logits\n","    # Sum logits of the last token to get a scalar output for attribution\n","    return logits[:, -1, :].sum(dim=-1)\n","\n","# Initialize embeddings\n","embedding_layer = lm_model.transformer.wte\n","input_embeddings = embedding_layer(input_ids)\n","\n","# Compute Integrated Gradients\n","ig = IntegratedGradients(predict)\n","attributions, delta = ig.attribute(inputs=input_embeddings, return_convergence_delta=True)\n","\n","# Aggregate attributions across embedding dimensions\n","attributions_sum = attributions.sum(dim=-1).squeeze(0)\n","\n","# Visualization using positional arguments\n","visualization.visualize_text([visualization.VisualizationDataRecord(\n","    attributions_sum.detach().numpy(),  # word_attributions\n","    torch.tensor(1),                    # pred_prob\n","    \"Generated Text\",                   # pred_class\n","    \"N/A\",                              # true_class\n","    \"Attribution\",                      # attr_class\n","    attributions_sum.sum().item(),      # attr_score\n","    tokenizer.tokenize(sentence),       # raw_input\n","    delta.item()                        # convergence_score\n",")])\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":213,"referenced_widgets":["47a2e5031bf648668608da87d079e3e8","f9d017f5877e479b80e38d7d2d3fee3f","fce683527b334f5793a9873751196d5f","36103fdecdc44ed79d53703884084b09","53cf6a467eb04bc88995920deb5888c9","341e2411ca004a859ea610329a817e22","b9f30bb3d54a4614b1aac3a17f7f2365","ea5004ad4f2d4accaf05eaf9bebdd675","f347148011c4430db421a68584250474","8f2397aaa9554e9184b3e4f46acf1b2a","6d0699f1c92748c98cd0bd187cc0a311"]},"id":"pS0bUQ2Zl_oZ","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1757427887379,"user_tz":-420,"elapsed":10599,"user":{"displayName":"Harriet","userId":"08169952984174915407"}},"outputId":"94f92d71-4f30-45fb-c64f-5c836b7c4360"},"execution_count":6,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["generation_config.json:   0%|          | 0.00/124 [00:00<?, ?B/s]"],"application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"47a2e5031bf648668608da87d079e3e8"}},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<IPython.core.display.HTML object>"],"text/html":["<table width: 100%><div style=\"border-top: 1px solid; margin-top: 5px;             padding-top: 5px; display: inline-block\"><b>Legend: </b><span style=\"display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px;                 border: 1px solid; background-color:                 hsl(0, 75%, 60%)\"></span> Negative  <span style=\"display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px;                 border: 1px solid; background-color:                 hsl(0, 75%, 100%)\"></span> Neutral  <span style=\"display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px;                 border: 1px solid; background-color:                 hsl(120, 75%, 50%)\"></span> Positive  </div><tr><th>True Label</th><th>Predicted Label</th><th>Attribution Label</th><th>Attribution Score</th><th>Word Importance</th><tr><td><text style=\"padding-right:2em\"><b>N/A</b></text></td><td><text style=\"padding-right:2em\"><b>Generated Text (1.00)</b>